  "query": "I'm about to buy my first serious pair of headphones and I refuse to spend money on technology I don't understand. Everyone my age just assumes wireless, but my dad insists a cable will always sound better and that Bluetooth 'crushes' the music. How did we get from headphone jacks to everything being wireless, what actually happens to the audio when it goes over Bluetooth, and is the cable crowd still right today? Once I get the story, I'd like to know whether current buyers regret going one way or the other, and which pair you'd start me on.",
